e series consists mostly of freshly emerged specimens taken the same night with a blacklight trap at the type locality, which is an opening in a dry pine forest. All known specimens were collected in late June and July.","","text","",""]]},"RGCVH":{"d":[["Europe & Northern Asia (excluding China)","","text","",""]]},"RRPZL":{"d":[["Distribution. Endemic in China (Fujian, Guangdong, and Hong Kong).","","text","",""]]},"S6MQS":{"d":[["Distribution: The slope of Sea of Okhotsk near the western Kamchatka Peninsula in 200 – 460 m depth.","","text","",""]]},"S7NLV":{"d":[["Southern Asia","","text","",""]]},"SWY7":{"d":[["","AU","iso","",""],["","ID","iso","",""],["","MY","iso","",""],["","PG","iso","",""],["","SB","iso","",""]]},"T43HW":{"d":[["Distribution. Japan (Honshu and Shikoku).","","text","",""]]},"T787":{"d":[["Mexico","2224","mrgid","",""]]},"TZHK9":{"d":[["Distribution. Philippines (Luzon).","","text","",""]]},"V7HLY":{"d":[["Gyeongsangbuk-do","","text","",""]]},"V9QTF":{"d":[["China (Guangxi)","","text","",""]]},"VB3V9":{"d":[["Habitat in O. Asiae.","","text","",""]]},"VCCRL":{"d":[["MXE-NL","MXE-NL","tdwg","",""]]},"VCKBT":{"d":[["Geographic distribution. Termitoquedius andinus sp. nov. is known from the Department of Cochabamba, Bolivia, at an elevation of 1040 m. It occurs within the Rondônia province and about 6 km from the border with the Yungas province, both belonging to the South Brazilian dominion (sensu Morrone et al. 2022). The species occurs in close proximity to the Tropical Andes biodiversity hotspot (sensu Myers et al. 2000) (Fig. 4). This locality represent the first country record of the genus for Bolivia.","","text","",""]]},"VRYY":{"d":[["CU","CU","iso","",""]]}}